319	// §5  AMD-NATIVE device kernel (Stage 5 hand-written AMDGCN).
320	//
321	// The prodigy_reduce step: TWO parallel global sums computed in one pass,
322	// mirroring the sm_90 prodigy_reduce_kernel —
323	//   r_global = Σ_i g_i · (p_init_i − p_i) · d_prev     (numerator)
324	//   s_global = Σ_i d_prev² · |g_i|                       (|denominator|)
325	// then on the host: d_new = max(d_prev, r_global / (|s_global| + 1e-12)).
326	// Each thread accumulates BOTH partials, then we run TWO independent
327	// wave→block→AGENT-atomic trees (the standard 2-level tree from the spec):
328	//   1. each thread grid-strides, accumulating r_local and s_local;
329	//   2. amd::wave_reduce_add_dpp on each → per-wavefront r/s sums (§2.6);
330	//   3. lane 0 of each wavefront writes r/s to LDS slots; workgroup_barrier;
331	//   4. the first wavefront reduces both slot arrays via a second DPP reduce;
332	//   5. one thread does two amd::atomic_add_agent_f32 (to r_acc and s_acc)
333	//      (§2.13: AGENT-scope atomics, visible across all 8 XCDs of MI300X).
334	// APPLY: the per-element Adam apply (with d as the effective lr) stays on the
335	// ATen host path (launch_prodigy_step) — only the r/s reduction is AMDGCN.
336	// ============================================================================
337	namespace sg { namespace gfx942 { namespace native {
